{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cedfuf5NjyeVLB4WaoQ5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: needs_more_evidence\nCONSENSUS_BLOCKING: yes\nRATIONALE: The supplied evidence is after-state only. The core claim under attack — \"no routing behavior may change\" — cannot be adjudicated without the before-state of `run-empire-v2.js`'s ohlcHandler. Two substantive risks remain open: (1) `updateLastPrice(sym, ohlcData[5], ohlcData[1])` now feeds the monotonic time gate with broker event time; if the prior call used the `Date.now()` default (or didn't exist here), mark-acceptance semantics changed — and if `ohlcData[1]` is seconds while any other caller seeds `lastPriceTimes` with ms-epoch `Date.now()`, the gate `incomingTime < currentTime` silently rejects every broker-bar mark forever (trace would show `mark_unchanged` but mark state feeding getEquity and force-close pricing goes stale). (2) `StateManager.updateLastPrice` returning booleans is presented as context, but if those returns were added in this change it's a fourth touched file contradicting the three-file diff claim. The trace itself is honest on the routing question: `strategyEligible: tf === activeTf` uses the same captured const as the actual branch, no `strategyRouted` claim, and the test asserts ordering and single emission — but all tests are string-index tests over source text, not behavioral tests, and `handlerEnd` silently degrades to a near-whole-file slice if `this.sessionRouter.wire(` is not found.\nDISAGREEMENT: The CHANGELOG claim \"without changing routing behavior\" is unproven for mark-state behavior: switching the timestamp argument to `ohlcData[1]` (if that is a change) alters which updates the monotonic gate accepts, which is observable behavior in equity math and force-close pricing, not merely tracing.\nREQUIRED_RECHECK: git diff HEAD~1 -- run-empire-v2.js core/StateManager.js (or the branch-base diff) restricted to the ohlcHandler region and `updateLastPrice`; plus a receipt establishing the unit (ms vs seconds) of `ohlcData[1]` at its producer (SessionRouter normalization).\nRECHECK_PROMPT: \"Mercury: produce the before-state of the ohlcHandler in run-empire-v2.js for this diff. Answer with receipts: (1) Did `stateManager.updateLastPrice` get called here before this change, and with what arguments — specifically was `ohlcData[1]` passed or was the `Date.now()` default used? (2) Cite the SessionRouter normalization code that builds `ohlcData[1]` and state its unit (ms or seconds epoch). (3) Enumerate ALL other callers of `updateLastPrice` and the timestamp unit each passes — do not stop at the first caller. (4) Confirm with git blame whether the boolean `return true/false` statements in StateManager.updateLastPrice (core/StateManager.js:892-909) predate this diff. Cite file:line for every claim.\"\nNEXT_CHECK: `git log -p -1 -- run-empire-v2.js` plus `grep -n \"updateLastPrice(\" -r core/ brokers/ run-empire-v2.js` on the host to enumerate all callers and their timestamp units.\nCANDIDATE SET: examined 5 of 3 (M = 3 touched files per host manifest/CHANGELOG; 5 artifacts supplied). Candidates: (1) CHANGELOG.md:8-14 [touched], (2) run-empire-v2.js:923-976 [touched], (3) test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js:21-55 [touched], (4) core/StateManager.js:892-920 [context — touched-status unverified], (5) core/TraceSpine.js:313-324 [context]. NOT enumerable from here: other `updateLastPrice` callers, other `emitTrace('LAST_PRICE_INFLUENCE')` sites outside the handler slice, SessionRouter normalization producer of `ohlcData[1]`, `handleMarketData` downstream mark writes, the before-state of the handler.\nAST EVIDENCE: absence. The supplied test file uses `indexOf`/substring assertions over raw source text — no AST-capable scan was cited for run-empire-v2.js, StateManager.js, or TraceSpine.js, and no env-var/config-key scan exists in evidence. Zero cited AST evidence.\nINHERITED: run-empire-v2.js — `this.sessionRouter?.activeSession || 'unknown'` (×3, silent default on trace source, unfixed); `(this.timeframeSelector && this.timeframeSelector.currentTimeframe) || this.candleTimeframe` (silent trading-relevant timeframe fallback, unfixed); `eventSymbol || rawSymbol || '(missing)'` (silent default, unfixed); `if (stateManager && stateManager.updateLastPrice)` guard silently skips mark update with no distinct trace signal (unfixed). core/StateManager.js — `getLastPrice` returns `... || null`, coercing any falsy stored price to null (unfixed, mitigated by the >0 store guard). core/TraceSpine.js — silent early return when tracing disabled (by design, unfixed). test file — `handlerEnd` indexOf can return -1 yielding a degenerate near-full-file slice (unfixed). CHANGELOG.md — n/a.\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 4 of 4. (1) `if (stateManager && stateManager.updateLastPrice)` guard — producer-fixable (stateManager presence should be an invariant at this point; guard masks its absence as `mark_unchanged`). (2) `markUpdated ? 'mark_updated' : 'mark_unchanged'` — true boundary (trace-only labeling), but conflates guard-skip with monotonic rejection. (3) `activeTf` `||` fallback to `this.candleTimeframe` — producer-fixable silent default if newly introduced; inherited otherwise. (4) `updateLastPrice` early-return validation gates (context file) — true boundary input validation.\nALLEGATIONS: A1 SUBSTANTIVE/RECEIPT-gap — timestamp-unit mismatch risk in monotonic gate (`ohlcData[1]` unit unproven; StateManager code at HEAD is RECEIPT that mixed units would silently reject). A2 SUBSTANTIVE/TESTIMONY — \"no behavior change\" rests on the CHANGELOG entry (TESTIMONY); the before-diff receipt is absent. A3 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — `influence: 'mark_unchanged'` conflates \"no stateManager\" with \"rejected\", weakening the \"actual mark-update result\" claim. A4 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — tests are string-presence, not behavioral; no runtime test that non-active frames update mark and active-only frames route. A5 MECHANICAL/TESTIMONY — three-file claim vs. possible StateManager boolean-return addition (fourth file / scope drift) unverified. Per doctrine, TESTIMONY alone cannot raise found_break; hence needs_more_evidence, not found_break.\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION: none — there is no prior Mercury seat output to converge with or dispute; A1/A2 are open receipts-needed items, not seat disagreements.\nWHAT I EXAMINED: the five host-attested excerpts (CHANGELOG.md:8-14, run-empire-v2.js:923-976, test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js:21-55, core/StateManager.js:892-920, core/TraceSpine.js:313-324), the evidence manifest hashes/provenance, the Ruling 4 statement, and the prior-fixes ledger context.\nDID NOT EXAMINE: the before-state/unified diff of run-empire-v2.js; SessionRouter's normalization producing `ohlcData[1]`; other callers of `updateLastPrice`; `handleMarketData` internals; whether other `LAST_PRICE_INFLUENCE` emit sites exist outside the excerpt; git blame on StateManager returns; any host-attested test run receipt (none supplied — sandbox run_check declared non-authoritative and no result was provided anyway).\nASSUMED: the excerpts match HEAD as the manifest hashes attest; StateManager.js and TraceSpine.js are context files not part of the three-file diff; `stateManager` is a valid in-scope binding in the ohlcHandler closure; the handler is synchronous between the trace emit and the `if (tf === activeTf)` branch (no await visible in the excerpt)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17383,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17383},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[REDACTED]","uuid":"[REDACTED]","timestamp":"2026-09-02T00:34:04.152Z","request_id":"